# WHO and DOING once logged in (#2847, #2851, #2886): a name pattern lists only the players it names
# (a prefix, or with * or ? a wildcard over names and aliases), the newest connection comes first,
# and a control character in @doing shows as a space so each player keeps to one line.
::case who.pattern  WHO and DOING list only the players the pattern names
::login alice Alice alicepass
::login bob Bob bobpass
::as alice
WHO b
WHO *ic*
WHO *ob
DOING al
DOING ?ob

::case who.order  the newest connection is listed first
::as alice
WHO
DOING
::logout alice
::login alice Alice alicepass
WHO
::as bob
DOING

::case who.doing  a tab in @doing is shown as a space (%r is CRLF in PennMUSH, two spaces)
::as alice
&DOING me=first%tsecond
WHO al
DOING al
&DOING me
::logout alice
::logout bob
